              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A contract entry point grows a collection that was read from storage without checking a length or capacity limit. Repeated calls can grow the ledger entry without bound, increasing rent and eventually making reads or iteration fail, a denial of service."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Unbounded collection growth in an entry point\n\nA contract entry point grows a collection that was read from storage without checking a length or capacity limit. Repeated calls can grow the ledger entry without bound, increasing rent and eventually making reads or iteration fail, a denial of service.\n\n### Remediation\n\nCap the collection size before growing it: read the current length and reject the operation at a documented maximum, or store a bounded aggregate instead. Return a typed contract error when the cap is reached.\n\n### References\n\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security/resource-limits",
                "text": "A contract entry point grows a collection that was read from storage without checking a length or capacity limit. Repeated calls can grow the ledger entry without bound, increasing rent and eventually making reads or iteration fail, a denial of service.\n\nRemediation: Cap the collection size before growing it: read the current length and reject the operation at a documented maximum, or store a bounded aggregate instead. Return a typed contract error when the cap is reached."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security/resource-limits",
