            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A public contract entry point makes a cross-contract call before its first storage write. Soroban permits reentrancy, so a malicious callee can be invoked while the caller's state still reflects the pre-call values and may re-enter or observe inconsistent state. This is a heuristic ordering check: it only compares call and mutation positions within the same function and cannot prove that reentrancy is reachable or exploitable."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Cross-contract call before state update\n\nA public contract entry point makes a cross-contract call before its first storage write. Soroban permits reentrancy, so a malicious callee can be invoked while the caller's state still reflects the pre-call values and may re-enter or observe inconsistent state. This is a heuristic ordering check: it only compares call and mutation positions within the same function and cannot prove that reentrancy is reachable or exploitable.\n\n### Remediation\n\nFollow checks-effects-interactions: validate inputs, update all relevant contract state, and only then invoke another contract. If an external call must happen first, add an explicit reentrancy guard and document why the intermediate state is safe to observe.\n\n### References\n\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs",
                "text": "A public contract entry point makes a cross-contract call before its first storage write. Soroban permits reentrancy, so a malicious callee can be invoked while the caller's state still reflects the pre-call values and may re-enter or observe inconsistent state. This is a heuristic ordering check: it only compares call and mutation positions within the same function and cannot prove that reentrancy is reachable or exploitable.\n\nRemediation: Follow checks-effects-interactions: validate inputs, update all relevant contract state, and only then invoke another contract. If an external call must happen first, add an explicit reentrancy guard and document why the intermediate state is safe to observe."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security",
              "id": "SS-013",
              "name": "Cross-contract call before state update",
              "properties": {
