              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A contract entry point mutates storage before calling `require_auth`. The authorization check must run before the effect, otherwise a rejected call may already have changed state on some paths and the ordering indicates a logic bug."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Authorization after state mutation\n\nA contract entry point mutates storage before calling `require_auth`. The authorization check must run before the effect, otherwise a rejected call may already have changed state on some paths and the ordering indicates a logic bug.\n\n### Remediation\n\nAuthorize the caller at the start of the entry point, before any storage read or write that depends on the caller. Call `require_auth` or `require_auth_for_args` first, then perform the state change.\n\n### References\n\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security/authorization",
                "text": "A contract entry point mutates storage before calling `require_auth`. The authorization check must run before the effect, otherwise a rejected call may already have changed state on some paths and the ordering indicates a logic bug.\n\nRemediation: Authorize the caller at the start of the entry point, before any storage read or write that depends on the caller. Call `require_auth` or `require_auth_for_args` first, then perform the state change."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security/authorization",
              "id": "SS-017",
              "name": "Authorization after state mutation",
              "properties": {
