              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A public contract entry point is named like a test or debug backdoor (a `test`, `debug`, `dev`, `mock`, or `dummy` name segment). Backdoor entry points that remain callable in a production deployment let anyone invoke privileged behavior, and are a well-known way on-chain contracts are compromised. This is a name-based heuristic and may flag a legitimately named function."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Public test or debug hook in a contract entry point\n\nA public contract entry point is named like a test or debug backdoor (a `test`, `debug`, `dev`, `mock`, or `dummy` name segment). Backdoor entry points that remain callable in a production deployment let anyone invoke privileged behavior, and are a well-known way on-chain contracts are compromised. This is a name-based heuristic and may flag a legitimately named function.\n\n### Remediation\n\nRemove test/debug entry points before deployment, or gate them behind `#[cfg(test)]` or a compile-time feature so they cannot be called from a production build. Never ship a privileged function intended only for testing.\n\n### References\n\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security",
                "text": "A public contract entry point is named like a test or debug backdoor (a `test`, `debug`, `dev`, `mock`, or `dummy` name segment). Backdoor entry points that remain callable in a production deployment let anyone invoke privileged behavior, and are a well-known way on-chain contracts are compromised. This is a name-based heuristic and may flag a legitimately named function.\n\nRemediation: Remove test/debug entry points before deployment, or gate them behind `#[cfg(test)]` or a compile-time feature so they cannot be called from a production build. Never ship a privileged function intended only for testing."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security",
              "id": "SS-029",
              "name": "Public test or debug hook in a contract entry point",
              "properties": {
                "category": "access-control",
                "confidence": "medium",
                "references": [
                  "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security"
                ],
                "remediation": "Remove test/debug entry points before deployment, or gate them behind `#[cfg(test)]` or a compile-time feature so they cannot be called from a production build. Never ship a privileged function intended only for testing.",
                "severity": "medium"
